Z||000000||Philphine||10-03-2001||10:59 PM||||i am just about finished with the speaker pods for my gt. a while back when i was doing pods for my truck, i sprayed them with undercoating to give them a vinyl like looking texture (i also thoght it would be a little like a sound deadener too) then i painted them. but after a while the paint kind of peeled off like it didn't adhere. i like the idea though so i'm wondering if i could get it to work if i used primer this time before paint. or would truck bedliner work better? i don't know if they are two different materials or not. possibly even one of those colored bedliner sprays (if i could find gray)?<P>anyone ever tried painting either and did you have to do anything special? thanks for any help.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||10-04-2001||10:36 PM||||ok, so i got antsy and found the undercoating i used before. it says it's paintable so i used it again. i guess i just need to find out what type of paint to use and if i need primer. it says it's "rubberised" if that helps any.<P>no clues at all?<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||AutoXdbdragSE||10-04-2001||11:06 PM||||My expieriences with paintin over undercoating are poor.. the bedliner might be beter, but it still doesn't adhear to paint well..  You might try crackle finish paint, that would achieve the look your looking for<P>My pods are painted inside with just plain old titeseal rubberized undercoating and it really cuts down on standing waves and vibrations inside the box.. outside i used good ol bondo and krylon spray paint w/ clear<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://images.cardomain.com/installs/127000-127999/127806_27_full.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://images.cardomain.com/installs/127000-127999/127806_25_full.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by AutoXdbdragSE (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||10-04-2001||11:32 PM||||nice pods. are they free air or sealed? do the two speakers share the same air in the pod?||||reg||1
Z||000004||AutoXdbdragSE||10-04-2001||11:39 PM||||Sealed, the speakers don't share air, the 8 is in aproximatly a .67 cubic footer.. which is slightly small, and i'm just way to lazy to take the speaker out and put polyfill in.. and the top is like .13 cubic foot for the 6.5" midbass||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||10-06-2001||01:00 PM||||maybe you had some uncured resin on it or something. My experience is that rubberized undercoating sticks to almost anything.||||reg||1
